  "rationale": "Blocking backupHost:lateralMovement, jumpHost:lateralMovement, configSecret:credentialAccess and rdpLogin:authenticate makes the target unreachable. Blocking configSecret:credentialAccess also kills apiToken:authenticate, dbLogin:authenticate, ssoLogin:authenticate and printServer:lateralMovement, so domainAdmin:privilegeEscalation cannot be reached. Blocking jumpHost:lateralMovement kills serviceAccount:privilegeEscalation. Blocking rdpLogin:authenticate kills monitoringHost:lateralMovement and localAdmin:privilegeEscalation. As a result, all four parents of the target (vaultRead, codeRepo, shareMount, dbReplica) are blocked off. Three blocks are not enough: shareMount:collection needs its own block somewhere on the kerberoast -> backupHost -> shareMount chain. Each of the routes sshKey -> jumpHost -> codeRepo, rdpLogin -> monitoringHost -> dbReplica and configSecret/apiToken -> domainAdmin -> vaultRead needs a separate block that does not help with the others. That makes four blocks the minimum."
